+++ b/docs/FIGMA_REST.md
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+# Optional Figma REST tools through Solstice
+
+Prepared 2026-10-14 against Solstice MCP base `092b7b2`. This extension is disabled
+by default and has not been deployed or exercised against a real Figma account.
+It is a custom, read-only Figma REST integration. It does not proxy or impersonate
+`mcp.figma.com`, and does not provide the official Figma MCP design-context tools.
+
+## Contract
+
+The existing Auth0 verifier supplies the subject. No tool takes a subject, user,
+role, Figma token or arbitrary upstream URL. Solstice access tokens stay at the
+Solstice gateway; a separate, subject-bound Figma OAuth grant authorizes REST calls.
+
+| Tool | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `solstice_figma_status()` | Live account verification; `connected:true` only after a successful `/v1/me` response matching the stored Figma account. Failure states distinguish missing grants from provider unavailability. |
+| `solstice_figma_connect()` | One-use gateway `authorization_url`, valid for 10 minutes; verifies the same Solstice identity in the browser before Figma consent. This changes OAuth state and is explicitly **not** annotated read-only. Invoke only from a human Connect action. |
+| `solstice_figma_get_file(file_key, node_ids?, depth=2)` | Figma file or node JSON under `data`, provenance and selectors; depth 1–10, at most 50 node IDs, 2 MiB provider JSON limit. Narrow selectors after a size error. |
+| `solstice_figma_get_images(file_key, node_ids, format='png', scale=1)` | Embedded MCP PNG images or SVG resources. `structuredContent.images` links each successful node to `content_index`, MIME, bytes, SHA-256 and canonical Figma provenance. Missing renders are explicit. |
+
+Images accept 1–8 nodes, scale 0.01–4, 4 MiB per image and 8 MiB aggregate before
+base64 encoding. Only HTTPS downloads from the exact built-in Figma CDN host set
+are accepted, with no redirects and no provider authorization header. Signed CDN
+URLs are not returned as durable provenance. Unknown CDN hosts fail closed; an
+operator must inspect provider changes before updating the allowlist. The server
+must permit at least 12 MiB MCP responses for maximum-size exports.
+
+## Before deployment
+
+1. Register a **Figma REST OAuth app** for the organization. A private published
+   app can serve members of that organization/team; draft apps are restricted to
+   the app owner and plan admins. Confirm the intended users are eligible. Public
+   distribution needs Figma's public-app approval process.
+2. Configure only `file_content:read` and `current_user:read`. The latter verifies
+   the linked account without trusting a cached flag. Figma's own file access
+   permissions remain authoritative; scopes do not grant access to new files.
+3. Register this exact redirect URI for the deployed gateway origin:
+   `https://api.solsticehealth.co/mcp/figma/callback`. For staging, register its
+   corresponding HTTPS origin with the same path and configure that exact URI.
+   No localhost or caller-supplied redirect is accepted by this gateway module.
+4. Keep the existing Solstice Auth0 issuer, audience and `mcp:connect` authorization
+   in place. Register a separate **regular web application** in that same Auth0
+   tenant for the gateway browser-identity step, using RS256 ID tokens and only
+   `openid`. Register the exact allowed callback:
+   `https://api.solsticehealth.co/mcp/figma/identity/callback` (or the configured
+   staging gateway origin with that same path). Its client ID/secret stay on the
+   gateway; configure `FIGMA_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` and `FIGMA_AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET`.
+   Enable the same identity connections as the MCP sign-in so both flows yield
+   the same immutable `sub`. Matching email addresses are never sufficient.
+
+   A Workbench OAuth client must be registered separately with Auth0,
+   including its exact allowed loopback callback and public-client/PKCE settings.
+   That registration does not register a Figma app and does not create a Figma grant.
+5. Provision a PostgreSQL database (the central auth DB can be reused) with a
+   least-privilege runtime role. Apply `migrations/20261014_figma.sql` explicitly
+   using the deployment migration role. The application validates schema version 1
+   and never creates production tables. SQLite is rejected outside explicit tests.
+6. Put the following settings in the gateway's secret/configuration manager:
+
+   ```text
+   FIGMA_ENABLED=true
+   FIGMA_AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=<registered gateway Auth0 regular-web-app client ID>
+   FIGMA_AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET=<host-only Auth0 web-app secret>
+   FIGMA_CLIENT_ID=<registered Figma REST app client ID>
+   FIGMA_CLIENT_SECRET=<host-only client secret>
+   FIGMA_REDIRECT_URI=https://api.solsticehealth.co/mcp/figma/callback
+   FIGMA_DATABASE_URL=<PostgreSQL URL, or omit to reuse CENTRAL_AUTH_DB>
+   FIGMA_VAULT_KEYS=<Fernet key, or comma-separated keyring newest first>
+   ```
+
+   Generate a vault key with `python -c 'from cryptography.fernet import Fernet;
+   print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())'` in the secret-provisioning environment.
+   Do not commit it, copy it to client configuration, or place it in tool logs.
+   Keys encrypt both grants and PKCE verifiers, with client/subject/purpose bound
+   inside the authenticated ciphertext. Back up the keys separately from the DB.
+7. Route `/mcp/figma/connect`, `/mcp/figma/identity/callback` and
+   `/mcp/figma/callback` to this gateway service over HTTPS. These browser routes
+   are public, but state alone cannot link an account: the Auth0 callback verifies
+   signed identity against the MCP subject, and both callbacks require the bound
+   browser cookie. No caller-supplied identity is accepted. Suppress/redact query
+   strings at the reverse proxy, load balancer and access-log layer, because OAuth
+   codes and states arrive in the callback URL. Responses are no-store,
+   no-referrer, fixed HTML with a nonce-protected `window.close()`, without echoing
+   code/state/provider errors or redirecting to caller-controlled destinations.
+8. Deploy, confirm readiness, then inspect tools/list through an authenticated
+   Solstice session. Until `FIGMA_ENABLED` is true and configuration/schema are
+   valid, the four Figma tools remain absent. Enable the Workbench connection UI
+   only after this gateway rollout. Do not treat local mocks as a live connection.
+
+## Grant lifecycle and limits
+
+Connect returns a one-use gateway ticket, not a transferable Figma grant URL.
+Opening it creates an independent Auth0 authorization-code + S256 PKCE flow with
+random state and nonce. The gateway verifies the ID token's RS256 signature,
+issuer, audience, expiry, nonce and exact subject match to the authenticated MCP
+caller. Only then does it create a separate Figma OAuth state and PKCE verifier.
+This prevents someone from sending their connect link to another person and
+linking that person's Figma grant to the sender's Solstice account.
+
+A pre-auth `__Host-solstice-figma-link` cookie binds the Auth0 callback, then rotates
+after successful identity verification to bind the Figma callback. It is Secure,
+HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, with a 10-minute expiry. A forwarded post-identity
+Figma URL cannot finish without that browser's cookie. One linking flow per browser
+is supported; a new flow supersedes its cookie. Both OAuth states and the initial
+ticket are single-use, encrypted and bounded by the original 10-minute deadline.
+Starting another connection invalidates earlier pending flows. Each callback
+consumes its state before token exchange, including failures or a bad cookie.
+Interrupted exchanges require a new Connect action; codes are never replayed.
+Callback success returns no token in the page or MCP response.
+
+PostgreSQL `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` serializes refreshes for a grant across server
+workers. Inserts use conflict-safe creation before locking. The stored access
+and optional rotated refresh tokens are replaced together after successful
+validation. If Figma omits a refresh token, the existing reusable token is kept.
+A request rejected after another worker refreshed reuses that newer access token.
+Lock waits are limited to 10 seconds; HTTP reads have connection/read timeouts,
+byte caps and a 30-second checked response budget. Failures are surfaced; there
+is no unbounded retry. A 401/403 permits one refresh/retry, since Figma may use 403
+for invalid tokens as well as file permission failures.
+
+Figma currently keeps one access token per app/account. The database therefore
+permits one linked Solstice identity per Figma account/app. Connecting that account
+under another Solstice identity fails rather than creating competing refresh
+owners. Do not share authorization URLs. To unlink administratively, delete that
+subject/app's grant and pending rows, then revoke the app in Figma if required;
+local deletion alone does not revoke a provider grant. There is no unlink tool in
+this initial scope. Key rotation: add a new key first, retain old decrypting keys,
+then explicitly re-encrypt existing rows before removing old keys. Losing a key
+requires reconnecting affected users.
+
+The integration has no Figma write APIs, official MCP session, organization-wide
+file discovery, arbitrary-URL fetch or automatic third-party billing. It reads
+only file keys selected by the caller within that caller's Figma permissions.
+HTML/SVG imported into a workspace remain untrusted artifacts and must use the
+Workbench's isolated preview route.
+
+## Verification and rollout checks
+
+Offline tests use a temporary SQLite database and mocked HTTP. They cover durable
+PKCE/state, replay/expiry, forwarded-link account-linking attacks, real signed
+OIDC claim/nonce checks, secure cookie rotation, subject isolation, encrypted
+grant binding, concurrent
+refresh from multiple service instances, refresh-token preservation/rotation,
+live-status failure, type/byte/URL/redirect guards, embedded PNG/SVG mapping,
+Auth0-protected tool calls and callback output secrecy. They do not demonstrate
+real PostgreSQL locking, registered Auth0/Figma apps, real account consent, external callback
+routing, Figma's current CDN response headers or production rate limits.
+
+Before enabling production, operators must apply the SQL migration in staging,
+run simultaneous refreshes from two gateway processes against PostgreSQL, exercise
+one real consenting account in a normal browser, verify callback query-log
+redaction, and confirm import of one PNG and one SVG through the Workbench. Check
+a different account cannot access the first account's grant and that file-level
+permission denial remains a denial. Do not forward Auth0 bearers to Figma.
+
+```sh
+uv venv .venv
+uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements-dev.txt
+.venv/bin/pytest -q tests/test_figma.py
+.venv/bin/pytest -q
+.venv/bin/ruff check src/solstice_mcp/figma.py src/solstice_mcp/tools/figma.py \
+  src/solstice_mcp/figma_identity.py src/solstice_mcp/settings.py src/solstice_mcp/app.py tests/test_figma.py
+```
+
+Primary references, checked 2026-10-14: [Figma OAuth apps](https://developers.figma.com/docs/rest-api/oauth-apps/),
+[scopes](https://developers.figma.com/docs/rest-api/scopes/),
+[file/node/render endpoints](https://developers.figma.com/docs/rest-api/file-endpoints/),
+[PKCE](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7636),
+[Auth0 regular web authorization](https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/authentication-and-authorization-flow/authorization-code-flow/add-login-auth-code-flow),
+[Auth0 PKCE token exchange](https://auth0.com/docs/api/authentication/authorization-code-flow-with-pkce/get-token-pkce).
